{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Illustrate referral programme earnings"},"description":"Illustrates potential Referral Fees under The Bitcoin Adviser's standard referral programme terms. Hypothetical inputs only; it never reads or estimates what a real referrer is owed, and a referrer's own agreement governs. Inputs: clientsPerMonth (0 to 100, default 2), btcPerClient (0.1 to 1000, default 3), years (1 to 20, default 4), existingBookBtc (0 to 100000, default 0, counts toward the 200 BTC whole-book threshold only). Out-of-range values are clamped and echoed. Each year's referrals count for that whole year; every client stays, pays and adds nothing; client fees follow the public schedule by each client's year (1% years 1 to 4, 0.75% years 5 to 8, 0.5% from year 9). The Referral Fee is 10% of fees received, and 20% on the whole attributed book once it reaches 200 BTC. Results are in BTC; btcPrice (USD; btcPriceUsd is accepted as an alias) adds a US dollar figure held constant and never changes the BTC figures. Not a forecast or a guarantee. mode is \"recurring\" (default) or \"advance\". terms is one of the versions in the schema; leave it out for the standard terms in force. Draft terms here are a preview, not terms in force. With mode \"advance\", firstDeposit (a date, default today in Sydney) and measuredBtc (0 to 1000, default 3 BTC) set the illustration. Recurring mode ignores them.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"btcPerClient":{"type":"number"},"btcPrice":{"exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"btcPriceUsd":{"deprecated":true,"description":"Alias of btcPrice, in USD.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"clientsPerMonth":{"type":"number"},"existingBookBtc":{"type":"number"},"firstDeposit":{"format":"date","pattern":"^(?:(?:\\d\\d[2468][048]|\\d\\d[13579][26]|\\d\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00